Attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is an independent reimplementation, in Rust, of the Mihon manga
reader for Android. It shares no code with it, but follows its feature set,
information architecture, and data model closely, and was written by reading
the upstream sources.

  Mihon — https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The built-in AnimeSama source (src/source/animesama.rs) is a port of the
Kotlin extension of the same name. Its request flow, selectors, and the way it
reconstructs a chapter list from the site's inline JavaScript were derived from
that implementation.

  keiyoushi/extensions-source — https://github.com/keiyoushi/extensions-source
  src/fr/animesama, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Neither project is affiliated with, nor endorses, this one.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party runtime dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The binary links a number of Rust crates, each under its own permissive
licence (MIT, Apache-2.0, or both). Run `cargo tree` for the full list, or
`cargo about`/`cargo deny` to generate a licence report.

On startup the application may load font files installed on the system (for
example Yu Gothic, Malgun Gothic, Microsoft YaHei or Segoe UI Symbol on
Windows) so that non-Latin titles render. Those fonts are read from their
installed location and are neither bundled nor redistributed.
